# Build-context allowlist by exclusion. A file that is not in the build context
# cannot be COPY'd into a layer, no matter what a later Dockerfile edit does — so
# excluding secrets HERE, rather than trusting each stage to not copy them, is the
# guarantee that an API key never ends up in an image layer. `.env` at the project
# root currently holds a real ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; it must never reach the daemon.
.env
.env.*

# Installed on the build side from package-lock.json; a host node_modules would
# be the wrong platform and would defeat the lockfile cache.
node_modules/

# History, not runtime input. Also the largest thing after node_modules.
.git/
.github/

# Build output, coverage, logs. dist/ is produced by the build stage from src/;
# a stale host dist/ must not shadow it.
dist/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store

# results/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is listed in .gitignore, but the six
# calibration-*.json receipts inside it are force-tracked and the README presents
# them as committed evidence. Nothing in src/ or test/ reads that directory — the
# CLI only writes new artifacts into it — so they are not a functional input to
# either image. They stay in the context so the runtime image can carry the same
# receipts the repository does (152K), and a fresh run inside the container lands
# next to the old ones exactly as it would in a checkout. Copying .gitignore's
# `results/` rule here would have silently stripped the receipts from the image.

# Not needed inside any stage.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
LICENSE
README.md
